        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Catalaunian Plains</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">20 June 451 CE, a date first proposed by J. B. Bury and accepted by many; some authors have proposed the first week of July or 27 September, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hydatius">Hydatius</a>'s chronicle secures the battle to June</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Somewhere on the Catalaunian Plains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalons-en-champagne">Châlons-en-Champagne</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troyes">Troyes</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>; the site is disputed, and the ridge at Montgueux, west of Troyes, is the most thoroughly researched proposal</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">A coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a>, Alans and other allies under the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Flavius Aetius</a> and the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-i">Theodoric I</a>, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> and their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>; no reliable strengths survive, and modern estimates for the allied Germanic forces run under 50,000 and for Attila's army closer to 70,000</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-i">Theodoric</a> was killed and both sides suffered heavy losses. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>; whether the battle was a Roman and allied victory or an indecisive one is disputed.</span></div>
        </div>
